# TodoTask IDE Rules

## Source Of Truth

- Must follow `/Users/zyr/code/todotask/docs/baseline.md` as top authority.
- Check `/Users/zyr/code/todotask/docs/dev-phases.md` before starting implementation.
- Use `pnpm` only. Do not use `npm` or `yarn`.

## Frontend Rules (Vue3 + TS)

- Scope: all files under `packages/frontend/`.
- Must use Vue 3 `<script setup lang="ts">`; Options API is forbidden.
- Business code must be TypeScript; no `.js` business files.
- No `any`; use precise types, `unknown`, and narrowing when needed.
- Component file names must be PascalCase; use PascalCase in templates too.
- Composables must use `use` prefix; event handlers must use `handle` prefix.
- Do not place `v-if` and `v-for` on the same element.
- Do not use array index as `v-for` key; use stable business id.
- Router views should use lazy loading: `() => import('@/views/...')`.
- Prefer Tailwind CSS; use Less only for complex styling.
- Scoped component styles must use `scoped`; use `:deep()` for child penetration.
- Import order: Vue core -> third-party -> stores -> composables -> components -> types/utils/api.

## Backend Rules (Go + Gin + MongoDB)

- Scope: all files under `packages/backend/`.
- Keep strict layer direction: Handler -> Service -> Repository only.
- Handler: parse input, call service, map errors to HTTP status.
- Service: business orchestration and business errors.
- Repository: MongoDB CRUD only, no business logic.
- Do not ignore errors (no `result, _ := ...`).
- Do not log with `fmt.Println`; use Zap structured logger.
- Use unified response package (`pkg/response`); avoid direct ad-hoc JSON response style.
- All DB operations must use `context.Context` with timeout control.
- No physical delete for business data; use soft delete.
- For model structs, keep both `bson` and `json` tags.
- No fire-and-forget goroutines that cannot be stopped.

## Git And Delivery

- Commit format: `<type>(<scope>): <中文说明>` and keep summary <= 25 chars.
- Do not `git push` unless explicitly requested.

